# Privacy Policy

**Effective date:** August 3, 2026

This privacy policy covers the personal automation tool ("the App") used to
post pins to Pinterest on behalf of its single owner/operator.

## What this App does

The App is a personal-use script that connects to the Pinterest API to
create pins on the operator's own Pinterest account, linking to Amazon
products via the operator's Amazon Associates affiliate links.

## Data the App accesses

The App uses Pinterest's OAuth API to obtain an access token scoped to the
operator's own Pinterest account. It uses this token only to:

- Read the operator's own board list
- Create pins on the operator's own boards

The App does not access, collect, or store data belonging to any other
Pinterest user. It does not collect personal data from visitors, customers,
or any third party.

## Data storage

Access and refresh tokens are stored locally in an environment file on the
operator's own machine and are never transmitted to any party other than
Pinterest's API.

## Third parties

The App sends pin content (image, title, description, and an Amazon
affiliate link) to Pinterest's API for the sole purpose of publishing pins.
No data is shared with any other third party.

